1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:28,340
Good morning, Canvas community, how are we doing this morning?

2
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:36,400
Man, I was excited about my message, but I got even more pumped through worship this morning.

3
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:38,780
So hopefully that is the same for you guys.

4
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:44,180
If we haven't had the privilege to meet yet, my name is Corey Smith and I happen to be part of the teaching team here at Canvas.

5
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:49,640
I've got a ton to cover this morning, so let's jump into it.

6
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,420
Let's pray and then we'll jump into it. Sound good, church?

7
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:59,640
Dear Heavenly Father, we come to you today fully expecting that you'll reveal something new to our hearts about you today, Lord.

8
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:08,560
That you'll bestow us with more courage and comfort as we apprentice and conform to the image of your son, Jesus.

9
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:14,000
Lord, I ask that you soften hearts today to our topic.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,140
If it be from you, Lord, take me out of the way so the Spirit can speak through me.

11
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:25,740
I pray that the Father of our Lord Jesus, who gives us the spirit of wisdom today and reveals the more knowledge of him.

12
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:30,260
I pray that our hearts be enlightened so that we may live into the hope of our calling.

13
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:33,860
We thank you for the glorious inheritance promised to the saints.

14
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:36,700
Lord, for those hurting today, we ask for healing.

15
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:40,900
Lord, for those anxious today, we pray for peace.

16
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,640
We pray all of this for your glory and our neighbor's good.

17
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,740
And in the mighty name of Jesus, amen.

18
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:55,840
So, this week we'll be covering the question, why does God need to create a new heaven and a new earth?

19
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,940
Why couldn't he just do one or the other?

20
00:01:57,940 --> 00:02:07,260
This week we'll sort of act as a part two to Ryan's sermon last week, which was this idea of present reality in light of the present truth.

21
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:08,740
Apocalypse, right?

22
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:16,120
The unveiling of what's going on behind the scenes to comfort the church and being able to see behind the veil.

23
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:22,840
If you haven't been here, we took some questions from the congregation and we prepared some sermons around those questions.

24
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:25,200
This is one of those sermons.

25
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:28,300
So, this week we'll be covering the topic of new heavens, new earth.

26
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:35,120
And we'll be sitting with this idea of why does God need to create a new heaven and new earth?

27
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,720
Why couldn't he just do one or the other?

28
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:41,200
And I'm going to paraphrase my whole sermon with this.

29
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:45,660
I don't know why God does anything, which is why he's God and I'm not, amen.

30
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:52,540
But this question is a great teaching point and it's something I'm very passionate about.

31
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:59,660
So, the Bible uses these ideas of heaven and earth as ways to express thoughts about God's realm and our realm.

32
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:02,660
Heaven for God's realm, earth for our realm.

33
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:09,180
So, my goal in answering this question today is why in the end does God need to create a new heaven and new earth?

34
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:11,080
Why couldn't he just do one or the other?

35
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,780
But let's set the stage here.

36
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:15,520
What does the Bible say about heaven?

37
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:18,080
What does the Bible say about earth?

38
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:21,240
And what part does all that play into this?

39
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:23,040
We all know what the earth is like, right?

40
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,640
We can work from experience there.

41
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:28,720
But I think we have some assumptions as a church of what heaven's like.

42
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:31,900
So, let's check those against the source text.

43
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:37,360
Pop culture, philosophies, entertainment love to disciple us on what heaven is like.

44
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:42,460
But is that how the Bible prepares and sets the stage for God's ultimate plan of restoration and reconciliation?

45
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:52,640
Is the ultimate plan for redemption to whisk us off to the sky, to a celestial candy land of sorts, where we all live in a mansion in the clouds and we all get everything we didn't get in this earthly life?

46
00:03:52,640 --> 00:04:02,200
Where we all drive expensive cars, we all fish all day, we all golf all day, or whatever we want to do, somehow for the glory of God.

47
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:06,640
Some of my friends actually had a running joke for a while about a country song.

48
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:11,520
And it's kind of a, we weren't making fun of the song as much as we were the theology.

49
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,400
We used to say, decent song, terrible theology.

50
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,840
But the songs, the lyrics go like this.

51
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:19,640
Yeah, I believe them when they say you're in a better place.

52
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:22,200
You had a wild side, but you had amazing grace.

53
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:24,460
I know you're way off up in them clouds.

54
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:29,180
So, if you could still hear me right now, I hope you hit those gold streets on two wheels.

55
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:34,880
I hope your mansion in the sky has got a 10-acre field with some mud and some hubs you can lock in.

56
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:46,160
I think if we're all intellectually honest with ourselves, this weird picture of heaven that some people have in their minds doesn't actually fit in alignment with the God of the Bible.

57
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:48,580
And confession time.

58
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:55,400
This is my hesitation or even frustration sometimes when I talk about heaven or somebody talks to heaven with me.

59
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:57,180
Sometimes, not all the time.

60
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:58,260
Let me put that paraphrase out there.

61
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:05,620
Sometimes it feels like, when it's described, it feels like a Hallmark movie or a romantic comedy.

62
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:08,780
And if you like those things, great.

63
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:11,720
To me, they just feel cheap.

64
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:12,280
Right?

65
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:13,580
They don't unpack it.

66
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:18,460
They don't build to life the nuance and the complexities of our existence here.

67
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:22,000
And I, for one, just don't think God is cheap.

68
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:29,820
And I definitely don't think his plan for ultimate reconciliation is to evacuate us out of the world and to plop us in a cloudy place where we get everything we've ever wanted.

69
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:32,540
That just feels cheap.

70
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,580
Let me elaborate a bit more.

71
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:36,040
I know I'm poking a little bit.

72
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:38,960
Maria Shriver wrote in a book in 1999 called What's Heaven?

73
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:44,380
And I think this excerpt encapsulates Western thinking and even some in the church around this idea.

74
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:48,400
Heaven, Shriver says, heaven is somewhere you believe in.

75
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:52,440
It's a beautiful place where you can sit on soft clouds and talk to other people who are there.

76
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:56,660
At night, you can sit next to the stars, which are the brightest of anywhere in the universe.

77
00:05:56,660 --> 00:06:00,100
If you're good throughout your life, then you get to go to heaven.

78
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:04,660
When your life is finished here on earth, God sends angels down to take you up to heaven to be with him.

79
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:06,420
And grandma's with me.

80
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,840
Most importantly, she taught me to believe in myself.

81
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,660
And she's watching us from up there.

82
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:16,320
And I fear, it's the caricature, but I feel this is what the world thinks.

83
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:20,320
And even some Christians just replace the line, if you're good throughout your life, then you get to go to heaven with.

84
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:22,920
If you believe in Jesus, then you get to go to heaven.

85
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:27,680
That would be the only real distinction about how Maria Shriver describes it.

86
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:31,840
See, I would strongly argue that this is not the biblical idea of heaven at all.

87
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:36,000
And if this is your first time joining us, you're welcome here.

88
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:42,380
Surprisingly to some people, the phrase going to heaven when you die is nowhere in the biblical text.

89
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:49,220
And many Christians assume that whenever the New Testament speaks of heaven, it refers to the place to which the save will go immediately after death.

90
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,260
But the language of the New Testament doesn't work that way.

91
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:58,560
Usually when heaven is referred to, it's referred to as the kingdom of heaven or even the kingdom of God.

92
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:09,500
This kingdom language that Jesus is referring to and preaching about is not our escape from this world into another one, but that God's sovereign rule is coming to earth as it is in heaven.

93
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:24,200
See, the roots of this misunderstanding go very deep, not least of all the philosophy of Plato that have seeped into our Christian worldview and that has taught us to devalue our bodies and devalue the present world as shameful or shabby.

94
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:37,040
Randy Alcorn calls this Christoplatonism, where we can have this Platonist idea, this philosophy, where our souls occupy our bodies like a hermit crab occupies a shell.

95
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:40,780
Christoplatonism is not a good thing.

96
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:45,420
It's actually a bad thing when we have a common philosophy that we transpose over the Scriptures.

97
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:47,020
Right?

98
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:54,000
For Christians, the question is not, do we have, and I may be stepping on some toes here, but bear with me.

99
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:58,100
For Christians, the question is not, do we have a soul or a body?

100
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:06,360
But the biblical fact is that we are both a soul and a body, a spiritual nature as well as a physical one.

101
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:09,760
God created us that way in a sort of cosmic unity.

102
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:14,200
It should never be an either or, but a both and.

103
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:16,340
Matthew Lee Anderson puts it well.

104
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:33,820
See, if we believe even subconsciously that the material world, this material world is inherently unspiritual, catch that.

105
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:46,660
If we believe this material world is unspiritual, just like when we separate body and soul, we will begin to ignore or even spiritualize the idea of resurrection.

106
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:51,880
Some people speak of a spiritual resurrection and not a physical one.

107
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:57,840
But just as a sunrise requires a sun, so too does resurrection require a body.

108
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,580
That's what resurrection means.

109
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:07,880
The resurrected Jesus assured his disciples in Luke 24, touch me and see me because a ghost doesn't have flesh or bones, as you can see I have.

110
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:12,480
Yet, right, I'm picking on us here, right?

111
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:16,860
Yet, even there's some evangelicals that imagine that we turn into ghosts.

112
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:19,740
This is the danger.

113
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:24,680
The very thing that we turn into ghosts, the very thing Jesus reassured his disciples he was not.

114
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:28,900
This is the danger of separating the spiritual and physical aspects of our creative world.

115
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:32,620
The good news is, this is not the narrative of the Scripture.

116
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:36,780
We are not destined for a disembodied existence.

117
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:43,080
In fact, the pictures of heaven in Revelation, especially Revelation 4 and 5, which Ryan preached about last week,

118
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:46,540
where the 24 elders are casting their crowns before the throne of heaven,

119
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:51,360
beside the throne of God and the Lamb, beside the sea of glass,

120
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:56,680
is not a picture of the last day where all the redeemed are in an ethereal heaven at last,

121
00:09:56,680 --> 00:10:03,480
but instead is a picture of present reality, the invasion of the heavenly dimension into our present life.

122
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:06,860
Heaven in the Bible is not just a future destiny.

123
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:11,560
But it is the other hidden dimension of our ordinary lives.

124
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:14,560
God's dimension, if you'd like.

125
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:20,440
God made heaven and earth in Genesis 1, and at last he will remake and join them both together forever.

126
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:24,960
See, when we come to this picture, the last two chapters in the Bible,

127
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:28,440
we don't find ransomed souls making their way to a disembodied heaven,

128
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:33,500
but rather we find the new Jerusalem coming down from heaven to earth,

129
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:39,260
uniting the two spheres in an everlasting embrace, the way God designed them to be.

130
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:43,640
God never changes, but heaven and earth will.

131
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:46,920
Randy Alcorn says this in an article I read,

132
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:52,400
we err when we confuse the present pre-resurrection heaven with the future post-resurrection heaven

133
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,500
that God will bring down to the new earth.

134
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:58,100
The present heaven is far better, according to Philippians 1.23,

135
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:01,020
than our lives under the curse of sin and suffering.

136
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:05,020
Upon death, we will be at home with the Lord, says 2 Corinthians 5.8.

137
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:07,920
But my point is, wonderful though as it may be,

138
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:12,220
we should not think of this present heaven as if it were our ultimate home.

139
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:14,240
The best is yet to come.

140
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:17,060
An eternal and delightful life,

141
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:18,960
worshiping and serving forever,

142
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:22,240
incarnate Jesus on the new and redeemed earth.

143
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:26,500
See, God made us both spirit and body the first time, right?

144
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,080
You and I are spirit and body.

145
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:32,580
Why do we think that plan changed?

146
00:11:32,580 --> 00:11:36,640
See, what we say about death and resurrection

147
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:39,140
gives shape and color to everything else.

148
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:43,880
If we're not careful, we offer merely a hope that is no longer a surprise,

149
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:47,380
no longer able to transform lives and communities in the present,

150
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:51,440
no longer generated by the resurrection of Jesus of himself

151
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,180
and looking forward to a new heaven, new earth.

152
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:58,480
The resurrection of Jesus changed the way the disciples saw their lives here.

153
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:00,440
It transformed them.

154
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:03,500
And I believe it still has that same transforming power today.

155
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:06,320
See, when they saw the resurrected Jesus,

156
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:08,940
the promise and hope that we should live in,

157
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:11,160
in the same way their tomb was empty,

158
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,780
So too will our graves be.

159
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:18,060
Our bodies, our physical bodies, albeit glorified,

160
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:20,920
will rise to worship from those graves

161
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,840
in an earthly, fully redeemed,

162
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:26,940
in an earth, fully redeemed with God as its rightful king.

163
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:30,520
See, I prayed this sermon wasn't seen as contentious,

164
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:33,740
but instead inspiring for all of you as it was for me

165
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,060
when I dove into this topic.

166
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:38,420
New heaven, new earth, resurrected bodies,

167
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:42,600
the God of the universe dealing final blows to enemies like sin,

168
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,480
injustice, and ultimately death itself.

169
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:49,000
Correcting and redeeming plan A,

170
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,640
which God is always in the business of doing.

171
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,900
See, where we don't sidestep our problems

172
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:57,400
and we teleport to a world somewhere else,

173
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:59,440
but where we have front row seats

174
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:02,720
to see God confront those problems head on,

175
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,920
either with our participation as the church

176
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:07,440
or him alone striking the final blow like only he can do.

177
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:10,200
See, the Scripture, in fact,

178
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:13,600
teaches things about the future resurrected life

179
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:16,080
that most Christians and almost all non-Christians

180
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:17,440
have never heard of.

181
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:20,220
I've prepared some heavy Bible reading today,

182
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:22,920
so without further ado, let's jump into the text.

183
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:25,260
We're going to start in Revelation 21,

184
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:29,640
and we are going to read all the way to Revelation 22, 5,

185
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:31,620
so hang on.

186
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:36,940
Then I saw a new heaven and a new earth,

187
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:40,840
for the first heaven and the first earth had passed away,

188
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,640
and the sea was no more.

189
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:45,720
I also saw the holy city, the new Jerusalem,

190
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:48,300
coming down out of heaven from God,

191
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,480
prepared like a bride adorned for her husband.

192
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:52,240
I listened to a sermon by Timothy Keller

193
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:52,980
where he says,

194
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:54,920
this changed my theology about heaven,

195
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:56,700
these two words, coming down.

196
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:59,660
Then I heard a loud voice from the throne saying,

197
00:13:59,660 --> 00:14:01,800
look, God's dwelling is with humanity,

198
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,580
and he will live with them.

199
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:05,400
They will be his disciples,

200
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:07,040
and God himself will be with them,

201
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,900
and will be their God.

202
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:11,380
He will wipe every tear from their eyes.

203
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:12,900
Death will be no more.

204
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:16,020
Grief, crying, and pain will be no more,

205
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:18,240
because the previous things have passed away.

206
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:20,620
Then the one seated on the throne said,

207
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:23,220
look, I am making everything new.

208
00:14:23,220 --> 00:14:27,000
He also said, right, because these words are faithful and true.

209
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,940
Then he said to me, it is done.

210
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,340
I am the alpha and the omega,

211
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:31,280
the beginning and the end,

212
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:33,160
and I will freely give to the thirsty

213
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,740
from the spring of the waters of life.

214
00:14:34,740 --> 00:14:37,120
The one who conquers will inherit these things,

215
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,560
and I will be his God,

216
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:40,400
and he will be my son.

217
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:41,820
But the cowards,

218
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:42,500
faithless,

219
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:43,300
detestable,

220
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:43,760
murderers,

221
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:44,540
sexually immoral,

222
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:46,480
sorcerers,

223
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:47,120
idolaters,

224
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,060
and all liars,

225
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:49,500
their share will be in the lake

226
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:50,980
that burns with fire and sulfur,

227
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:52,100
which is the second death.

228
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,540
Then one of the seven angels

